From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/50] ASoC: qdsp6: q6afe: send the DP stream and controller
 index

Before starting AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX (0x6020), the downstream kernel
for SM8150 phones sends two AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE parameters:

  AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG  stream index
  AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DPTX_IDX_CFG        DP controller (dptx) index

Mainline never sends them, and on this phone the DSP does not answer the start
of that port at all (-110).  Firmware built with DP MST support may need to
know which controller and stream feed the port before it can start it.

Send both, with index 0, before the port configuration.

What is verified against the downstream LineageOS reference source
(android_kernel_oneplus_sm8150, branch lineage-23.2; a downstream reference,
not proven to be the factory build):

 - techpack/audio/include/dsp/apr_audio-v2.h:
     line 3052  #define AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG     0x000102b5
     line 3053  #define AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DPTX_IDX_CFG           0x000102b6
     lines 2125-2133  struct afe_display_stream_idx { u32 minor_version;
                        u32 stream_idx; } __packed;
                      struct afe_display_ctl_idx { u32 minor_version;
                        u32 ctl_idx; } __packed;
   i.e. 8-byte payloads: two u32 words, minor version first and the index
   second.  Both parameters together are 16 payload bytes before their
   parameter headers - the layout used here, one parameter per SET_PARAM_V2.

 - techpack/audio/dsp/q6afe.c:6758-6834  afe_set_display_stream() packs both
   parameters with module_id = AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE, instance
   INSTANCE_ID_0 and minor_version = 1, and sends them to the port id.

 - techpack/audio/asoc/msm-dai-q6-hdmi-v2.c:331-361
   msm_dai_q6_hdmi_prepare() calls afe_set_display_stream() before
   afe_port_start(), only while the port is not already started.  On error it
   logs; if the error is -EOPNOTSUPP it carries on and starts the port, any
   other error aborts the prepare ("not starting AFE port").  stream_idx and
   ctl_idx are zero-initialised (kzalloc) and settable from the
   "Display Port RX DEVICE IDX" control, so index 0 is the downstream default,
   which is what this patch sends.

The payload struct is 8 bytes and carries a static_assert on that size, so a
future field or type change cannot silently change the wire format.

What is NOT verified and must not be assumed:

 - That the guacamole ADSP firmware accepts these parameters, or needs them.
   No hardware was available; this patch exists to find out.
 - That two separate SET_PARAM_V2 commands (mainline q6afe_port_set_param_v2)
   are equivalent to downstream's single SET_PARAM carrying both parameters.
   The per-parameter payload is identical; whether firmware cares about the
   packaging is unknown.
 - That the order relative to the port configuration matters.  Downstream's
   order is: display-stream parameters, then config, then start; this patch
   matches that order, but only the start boundary is sourced.
 - Anything about DP MST: both indices are 0 and mainline does not use MST.

Divergence from downstream: downstream aborts the prepare for any error other
than -EOPNOTSUPP, while this patch only warns and continues for every error, so
that one rejected parameter cannot mask the port-start result the experiment is
trying to observe.  To match downstream exactly, replace the dev_warn() with
"if (ret && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP) return ret;".

Inert unless the DisplayPort audio link is enabled: this runs only when a
stream is started on port 0x6020, so it cannot affect DP video or any other
audio path.  Drop the patch (remove from source=) if the DP audio logs show the
parameters rejected and nothing else changes.

Signed-off-by: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 182b68c..2010da9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
 #define AFE_SVC_CMD_SET_PARAM		0x000100f3
 #define AFE_PORT_CMDRSP_GET_PARAM_V2	0x00010106
 #define AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_CONFIG	0x00010210
+#define AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG	0x000102b5
+#define AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DPTX_IDX_CFG	0x000102b6
 #define AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE	0x0001020C
 #define AFE_MODULE_TDM			0x0001028A
 
@@ -79,6 +81,8 @@
 
 /* Port IDs */
 #define AFE_API_VERSION_HDMI_CONFIG	0x1
+/* DP stream/controller index parameters, same minor version downstream uses */
+#define AFE_API_VERSION_HDMI_DP_IDX_CFG	0x1
 #define AFE_PORT_ID_MULTICHAN_HDMI_RX	0x100E
 #define AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX	0x6020
 
@@ -424,6 +428,21 @@ struct afe_param_id_hdmi_multi_chan_audio_cfg {
 	u16 reserved;
 } __packed;
 
+/*
+ * Payload of AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG (0x102b5, the DP stream
+ * index) and AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DPTX_IDX_CFG (0x102b6, the DP controller
+ * index).  Both take the same shape: two u32 words, minor version first and
+ * the index second, so 8 bytes per parameter.  Downstream declares them
+ * separately as struct afe_display_stream_idx { u32 minor_version;
+ * u32 stream_idx; } and struct afe_display_ctl_idx { u32 minor_version;
+ * u32 ctl_idx; }, both __packed (techpack/audio/include/dsp/apr_audio-v2.h).
+ */
+struct afe_param_id_dp_idx_cfg {
+	u32 minor_version;
+	u32 idx;
+} __packed;
+static_assert(sizeof(struct afe_param_id_dp_idx_cfg) == 8);
+
 struct afe_param_id_slimbus_cfg {
 	u32                  sb_cfg_minor_version;
 /* Minor version used for tracking the version of the SLIMBUS
@@ -1667,6 +1686,37 @@ int q6afe_port_start(struct q6afe_port *port)
 	struct apr_pkt *pkt;
 	int pkt_size;
 
+	if (port_id == AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX) {
+		/*
+		 * Tell the DSP which DP stream and controller feed this port,
+		 * as the downstream kernel's afe_set_display_stream() does
+		 * before starting this port.  SM8150 has one DP controller and
+		 * mainline does not use MST, so both indices are 0.
+		 *
+		 * Downstream continues to the port start when the parameters
+		 * are rejected with -EOPNOTSUPP and aborts on any other error;
+		 * this only warns, so a rejection cannot hide the result of the
+		 * start the experiment is trying to observe.
+		 */
+		struct afe_param_id_dp_idx_cfg idx = {
+			.minor_version = AFE_API_VERSION_HDMI_DP_IDX_CFG,
+		};
+
+		ret = q6afe_port_set_param_v2(port, &idx,
+					      AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG,
+					      AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE,
+					      sizeof(idx));
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = q6afe_port_set_param_v2(port, &idx,
+						      AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DPTX_IDX_CFG,
+						      AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE,
+						      sizeof(idx));
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(afe->dev,
+				 "DP stream/controller index for port 0x%x: %d\n",
+				 port_id, ret);
+	}
+
 	ret  = q6afe_port_set_param_v2(port, &port->port_cfg, param_id,
 				       AFE_MODULE_AUDIO_DEV_INTERFACE,
 				       sizeof(port->port_cfg));
-- 
2.47.0

